"Agustina Victoria Ledezma - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/author/agustina-victoria-ledezma)\nciteturn6search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; ## Papers by Agustina Victoria Ledezma ... 2024-03-22 v2 ... On the diameter of Schrijver graphs\n\n2021-12-03 v2\n\nAgustina Victoria Ledezma, Adrián Pastine, Pablo Torres, Mario Valencia-Pabon\n\n# • INFO • BIB • PDF • ARXIV •\n\nOn the diameter of Schrijver graphs\n\nPublished • View Publication • BIB\n\nFor $k \\geq 1$ and $n \\geq 2k$, the well known Kneser graph $\\operatorname{KG}(n,k)$ has all $k$-element subsets of an $n$-element set as vertices; two such subsets are adjacent if they are disjoint. Schrijver constructed a vertex-critical subgraph $\\operatorname{SG}(n,k)$ of $\\operatorname{KG}(n,k)$ with the same chromatic number. In this paper, we compute the diameter of the graph $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ with $r \\geq 1$. We obtain an exact value of the diameter of $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ when $r \\in \\{1,2\\}$ or when $r \\geq k-3$. For the remained cases, when $3 \\leq r \\leq k-4$, we obtain that the diameter of $\\operatorname{SG}(2k+r,k)$ belongs to the integer interval $[4..k-r-1]$.\n\nchromatic number graph kneser\n\nMaintained by Per Alexandersson, per@symmetricfunctions.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAgustina Victoria Ledezma (https://www.csauthors.net/agustina-victoria-ledezma/)\nciteturn6search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; According to our database^{1}, Agustina Victoria Ledezma authored at least 2 papers between 2024 and 2025. ... On the diameter of Schrijver graphs.\n\n# Agustina Victoria Ledezma\n\nOrcid: 0000-0003-2491-1370\n\nAccording to our database^{1}, Agustina Victoria Ledezma authored at least 2 papers between 2024 and 2025.\nCollaborative distances:\n\n  * Dijkstra number^{2} of five.\n  * Erdős number^{3} of four.\n\n## Timeline\n\n#### Legend:\n\nBook  In proceedings  Article  PhD