x. A polynomial bound on polytope diameters is a necessary condition for a strongly polynomial simplex method, which is still unknown.\n\nTimeline of the conjecture before the counterexample:\n\n  * 1967, Klee and Walkup: the conjecture fails for unbounded polyhedra, and for bounded polytopes it is equivalent to the $d$d-step conjecture (the case $n=2d$n=2 d). They also proved it for $n-d\\le 5$n−d≤5.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPieter Schrijver - ID Oil Tools B.V. | LinkedIn (https://nl.linkedin.com/in/pieterschrijver)\nciteturn6search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Pieter Schrijver ... A 𝙈𝙪𝙡𝙩𝙞 𝘼𝙧𝙢 𝘾𝙖𝙡𝙞𝙥𝙚𝙧 gives clear internal geometry data: diameter changes, restrictions, deformation and ovality.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDiscrete Geometry · Prove2Me (https://prove2.me/f/discrete-geometry?status=completed)\nciteturn6search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Trivializing encodings are ruled out: the diameter is not `Metric.diam` (which is $0$0 on unbounded sets), rational unboundedness is not tested on $I_\\infty$I∞​ alone, periodicity requires $u \\ne 0$u=0, the index set is the projection of all of $M$M, and $k_1, k_2$k 1​,k 2​ are finite.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ns-stable Kneser graphs are Hamiltonian - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/%5C%28s%5C%29-stable_Kneser_graphs_are_Hamiltonian)\nciteturn6search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: last month; Ledezma, Adrián G. ...   * On the diameter of Schrijver graphs ... This page was last edited on 21 April 2026, at 00:34.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSurprises in Mathematics and Theory | Gödel's Lost Letter and P=NP (https://rjlipton.com/2009/09/27/surprises-in-mathematics-and-theory/)\nciteturn6search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 17.1 years ago; 